# Async Programming Patterns

## Channel Communication
- Use `tokio::sync::broadcast` channels for inter-component communication
- Buffer size is 8192 messages - monitor for overflow warnings
- Implement channel health checks in [src/channels.rs](mdc:src/channels.rs)

## Task Management
- Use `futures::try_join!` for concurrent task execution
- Implement graceful shutdown with proper error handling
- Use `tokio::time::interval` for periodic tasks

## Error Handling in Async Contexts
- Avoid blocking operations in async functions
- Use `tokio::time::timeout` for operations that might hang
- Implement proper error propagation through Result types

## Reconnection Patterns
- Implement exponential backoff for network reconnections
- Use `tokio::time::sleep` for delays between attempts
- Handle connection failures gracefully without terminating tasks

## Resource Management
- Use `Arc<Mutex<T>>` or `Arc<RwLock<T>>` for shared state
- Implement proper cleanup in async contexts
- Monitor resource usage to prevent memory leaks
